# in.npt_stability_supercell -- Stage D-2 worker fragment: single-stage NPT
# production MD on a SUPERCELL (~100-200 atoms), with per-species (Al vs Ni)
# MSD tracking to distinguish vibration from diffusion/melting.
#
# Deliberately single-stage (NPT only, no separate NVT thermalization) --
# explicit Stage D-2 instruction, unlike Stage D's NVT-then-NPT protocol.
#
# NOT standalone-runnable -- same reason as Stage D's in.nvt_stability /
# in.npt_stability (pair_style mliap unified EXISTS requires the
# Python-side lammps.mliap.load_unified_kokkos() call first; confirmed
# empirically, see those files' headers). Load via lmp.file() from
# lammps_stage_d2_run_phase.py AFTER read_data/model-load/pair setup on
# the SUPERCELL -- built by replicating each phase's own zero-stress
# PRIMITIVE cell (relaxed with the identical recipe Stage B/C/D used). A
# zero-stress primitive cell replicates to an exact zero-stress supercell
# by translational symmetry, so no separate supercell-scale relax is
# needed before this file runs.
#
# Driver must set these LAMMPS variables before lmp.file()'ing this script:
#   temp          target temperature, K
#   seed          velocity-seed RNG integer
#   tdamp         Nose-Hoover thermostat damping time, ps
#   pdamp         barostat damping time, ps
#   pressure      target external pressure, bar (0.0 = ambient)
#   npt_steps     number of 1-fs steps to run
#   thermo_every  thermo/log sampling interval, steps
#   final_data    path to write the post-NPT LAMMPS data file (provenance)
#
# Element order (fixed project-wide, ELEMENT_ORDER=["Al","Ni"], set by the
# driver's pair_coeff before this file runs): type 1 = Al, type 2 = Ni.

timestep 0.001

group grp_Al type 1
group grp_Ni type 2

# compute msd captures each group member's position AT THE TIME THIS
# COMMAND RUNS as x0 -- i.e. the just-relaxed 0 K lattice site, since this
# is issued before velocity create / before any dynamics -- and correctly
# unwraps displacement across periodic boundaries (LAMMPS compute msd
# documentation), so a rising trend reflects real diffusion, not an
# ordinary periodic-image wrap. c_msdAl[4]/c_msdNi[4] = total MSD
# (dx^2+dy^2+dz^2), averaged over each species group, in Angstrom^2.
compute msdAl grp_Al msd
compute msdNi grp_Ni msd

velocity all create ${temp} ${seed} mom yes rot yes dist gaussian

thermo ${thermo_every}
thermo_style custom step temp pe ke etotal press pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz lx ly lz xy xz yz vol c_msdAl[4] c_msdNi[4]
thermo_modify flush yes

print "=== STAGE D-2 NPT PRODUCTION START ==="
fix mdintegrate all npt temp ${temp} ${temp} ${tdamp} tri ${pressure} ${pressure} ${pdamp}
run ${npt_steps}
print "=== STAGE D-2 NPT PRODUCTION END ==="
unfix mdintegrate

write_data ${final_data} nocoeff
